Endless fog, clouds floating by,
But this eternity is just a beautiful lie.
Looking down from the edge, watching the waves,
Remembering the life that I couldn't save.
Cold air in my lungs, but I can't even breathe,
Fading in the shadows, begging to leave.
I’m a ghost in the dark, tryna find my way home,
In this silent kingdom, I'm forever alone.
Miss the warmth of the sun, miss the dirt on my feet,
This afterlife cold, man, it feels like defeat...
[Chorus]
(Style: Melancholic cloud rap, heavily echoed vocals, laid-back flow)
Wind blows through the bamboo, grey mist in my eyes,
No place for my soul under these hollow skies.
Take me back to the light, take me back to the start,
Before the cold took the beat from my heart...
[Verse 2]
(Style: The beat gets a bit wavey, shamisen plucks become rhythmic)
Then the mist cleared up, saw a neon glow,
Pink hair in the wind, moving soft and slow.
She was laughing at the waves, touching the tide,
Told me even in the dark, we don't have to hide.
A guide for the lost, with a smile so bright,
Turning all my shadows into warm, soft light.
She whispered: "Look close, see the ocean gleam?
Death is just the start of a different dream."
In her pink hair and her laugh, I found my release,
Letting go of the past, finally at peace.
No more running from the dark, no more pain in my chest,
Just wanted to stay in her neon nest...
[Bridge]
(Style: Atmospheric witch house drop, deep heavy bass, mystical echoes)
But she's a guide for the dead, she can't stay for long,
She healed my broken spirit with her silent song.
Walked back into the fog, fading out of my sight,
Looking for the other souls lost in the night.
Her pink shadow gone, back into the deep...
[Outro]
(Style: Whispered vocals, fading shamisen and flute)
Standing on the edge, watching clouds roll by.
No more tears in my eyes, no more asking why.
She is gone... but I'm not afraid.
I found my peace... in the home she made.
[End]